{
 "name": "FxKit",
 "made_by": "tools/blender/fx_kit.py",
 "frame": "Roblox studs, Y up. Each mesh is centred on its box; 'size' is that box at the unit size, and a MeshPart's Size scales it freely.",
 "use": "MeshPart.TextureID for the meshes (a warm pass preloads it; SurfaceAppearance can't be). The mesh textures are opaque and drawn in each palette's own colours: a fade is the part's Transparency, a silhouette is the mesh. The white textures are for Beams, Trails and particles, tinted by Color.",
 "burn": "Each coil also comes as 6 bands along its length, _Burn1 at the foot: place each band at the coil's centre plus its 'offset' times the coil's scale (Size over 'size'), and fade them foot first.",
